...
PR #499 introduces the CefPermissionHandler interface and PR #478 adds CefPermissionManager for the Alloy runtime. We should now add a CefPermissionHandler callback for the various APIs represented by blink::PermissionType.

With the Chrome runtime a client implementing this callback will be able to override the default user prompt behavior. Similarly, Chrome runtime support should be added for OnRequestMediaAccessPermission.

